Ave linux-ide folks

I've got a compile failure since 2.6.23-git15 which still isn't fixed in 
2.6.24-rc1

drivers/ide/pci/generic.c:70: error: generic_chipsets causes a section 
type conflict
make[3]: *** [drivers/ide/pci/generic.o] Error 1
make[2]: *** [drivers/ide/pci] Error 2
make[1]: *** [drivers/ide] Error 2
make: *** [drivers] Error 2

According to http://marc.info/?l=linux-ide&m=119317525632197&w=2 and 
http://marc.info/?l=linux-ide&m=119317525532195&w=2 more 
ide drivers have troubles when CONFIG_HOTPLUG=n.

Apparently the generic driver is also affected.
Both gcc 3.3 from debian stable as gcc 4.2.1 barf on the code.

Greetz Mu

